        <h6>Source of record</h6>
        <p>MoSPI / International Institute for Population Sciences (IIPS). National Family Health Survey, rounds 4 (2015-16) and 5 (2019-21). Retrieved via the eSankhyiki API (nfhs/getNfhsRecords), vintage <b id="prov-vintage">–</b>. All 21 indicators are ingested raw (data/raw/nfhs-records.json); seven thematic bundles carry the 102 All-India Combined sub-indicators with both survey values, plus 140 state-level cuts for NFHS-5.</p>
        <p><b>Methodological note.</b> Anaemia was measured with a different device in NFHS-5 (HemoCue Hb 301) than NFHS-4 (Hb 201+); blood-pressure thresholds were redefined. Where a methodological break is known it is disclosed on the chart. The two rounds are cross-sectional estimates compared by design; they are never chained and growth rates are not computed.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Revisions &amp; uncertainty</h6>
        <p>NFHS estimates are final on release. Sampling errors are published in the survey report; small states have wider confidence intervals. The survey covers ~600,000 households per round — large, but still a sample. NFHS-5 fieldwork was disrupted by COVID in its second phase (March-April 2021); the national estimate blends pre-pandemic and pandemic-period data.</p>
      </div>
